<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">bounties</ansi>

A bounty board in a town lists marks wanted in the lands around it: the
master of a lair, or a band of foes that keeps to the roads. Take a bounty,
go and kill the mark, and come back to any board to be paid in gold. The
proof is your company's chronicle (<ansi fg="command">help chronicle</ansi>), so a kill counts only if the
chronicle shows it.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bounty</ansi>                       the board you stand at, and the bounties you hold
  <ansi fg="command">bounty take [number]</ansi>         take a posting from the board
  <ansi fg="command">bounty claim [number]</ansi>        collect the gold for finished bounties (all of them, or one)
  <ansi fg="command">bounty drop [number]</ansi>         give up a bounty you hold
  <ansi fg="command">bounties</ansi>                     the same as <ansi fg="command">bounty</ansi>

The numbers are the ones on the board, or in your list of held bounties.
Taking and claiming happen at a board, in a room that has one (the Company
window's Bounties tab shows it as well, and it fits a phone). Reading what
you hold works anywhere.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The postings</ansi>

  Lair      slay the master of a lair in a named zone. It pays for one kill.
  Band      break three groups of a named kind in a named zone. A group is
            broken when every foe in it is down. While you hold the bounty,
            each one broken is written in your chronicle; other fights are
            not, so the chronicle keeps the deeds that matter.

Each posting names the zone's level band, and says how that band rates for
your company (<ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>). A bounty never changes a foe: the lair master and the
bands are exactly the ones the zone already has, at the zone's own level,
whoever takes the bounty. If you want a harder bounty, take one in a zone
above your level; if you want an easy one, take one near your level.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The board</ansi>

  - Each board posts up to five bounties from the zones near it, mostly bands,
    with a lair or two. A new list is posted every six hours, in real time;
    the board tells you how long is left. The same board always shows the
    same list within a window, through a restart or a copyover.
  - You can hold three bounties at once, and only one on a given mark. A held
    bounty lasts a day, whether you are logged in or not, then lapses.
  - Only what happens after you take a bounty counts. A kill from before does
    not, and neither does the same kill for a second bounty. A lair master
    must be slain, and a band broken, in the zone the bounty names.
  - A bounty you have claimed cannot be taken again from the same list.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The pay</ansi>

Gold only, by the zone's level band and no more: 20 gold times the band's
middle level for a lair master, and 6 gold per level for each band
broken (three bands). A level 8 zone (7-9) pays 160 for a lair and 144 for the
three bands. It is paid from your company's leader and comes with a line in
your chronicle (<ansi fg="command">chronicle bounties</ansi>). A bounty is a way to be paid for what you
would fight anyway: it adds no experience, loot or power, and a lair that
stays quiet after you beat it (<ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>) stays quiet for the bounty too.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help chronicle</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help regions</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>.
